1
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,580
传统的"开学日"薄烤饼
Traditional "First day of school" Pancakes.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:06,640
-画个奶油笑脸不 -老爸 我都上高中了
- Whipped-cream smile? - Dad, I'm in high school now.

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,720
直接挤进我嘴里就行
Just put it in my mouth.

4
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:09,960
好了 太恶心了 快住手
Okay, that's disgusting. Stop it.

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,540
快省省这发号施令的架势
Hey, save some of that bossing people around

6
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:12,540
留着去办公室使 女士
for the office, lady.

7
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,226
休假20年后
After a 20-year vacation,

8
00:00:15,226 --> 00:00:17,200
克莱尔终于要重回职场了
Claire is rejoining the work force.

9
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:17,780
那可不是休假
Not a vacation.

10
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:20,640
但我要去我爸的橱柜公司开始新工作了
But I am starting a job at my dad's closet company.

11
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:22,440
他打算栽培我日后接手公司
He's kind of grooming me to take over.

12
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:23,800
我有市场营销方面的专业背景
I have a background in marketing.

13
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,100
我非常为她骄傲
I'm so proud of her.

14
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:27,520
说到市场 我们家的牛奶喝完了
Oh, uh, speaking of marketing -- we're out of milk.

15
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,220
我其实挺紧张的
I'm actually kind of nervous.

16
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,160
你一定会表现得很好的
You're gonna be great.

17
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:32,380
记住 一旦碰到麻烦
And remember, if you get into a jam,

18
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,040
就来一段我教你的模仿秀
just do the impression I taught you.

19
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:38,260
嘿 你可以把你的衣服挂在我身体里
Hey. You can hang your clothes in me.

20
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:40,118
克里斯托弗-步入式衣柜
Christopher walk-in closet.

21
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,500
我死也不会那么做
I'm not doing that.

22
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,500
放松点 老妈 你是给外公干活
Okay, relax, mom. You're working for grandpa.

23
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:45,600
都算不上真正意义上的工作
It's not even a real job.

24
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:47,260
就跟夏天时 我给老爸打工一样
It's like that summer when I worked for dad.

25
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:49,220
他只是试图在帮我树立信心
He was just trying to make me feel good about myself.

26
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,300
不是真的需要我帮忙
He didn't really need my help.

27
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,000
不是这样的
That's not true.

28
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,960
我确实需要你帮我分发宣传单
I needed your help distributing all those fliers.

29
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:55,240
我确实也分了 看我眼色
And I did. Wink, wink.

30
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,960
你怎么现在就在做作业了
How are you already doing homework?

31
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:00,480
我都高三了 得考好点才行
It's junior year. I have to get good grades.

32
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,220
你不知道现在外面竞争多激烈吗
Don't you know how competitive it is out there?

33
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,080
别再给我施加压力了
Stop pressuring me!

34
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,420
好端端的小孩变成这副鬼样子
You know, this is what happens to kids

35
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:05,720
完全是因为缺乏性活动
when they're not sexually active.

36
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:07,300
你不用去学习吗
Don't you have some studying to do?

37
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,820
拜托 我上的是社区大学
Please, it's community college.

38
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:10,180
他们只会让你带根固体胶去上学
They tell you to bring a glue stick.

39
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:16,320
你好
Hello.

40
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:18,960
没错 就是他 那位 我
Yes, this is he -- him -- me.

41
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:19,860
第一次就说对了
Right the first time.

42
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:21,200
我马上过去
I'll be right there.

43
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,380
米奇尔 就是这个
Mitchell, that was it.

44
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:23,760
等的就是这电话 我要过去了
That was the call. I'm going in.

45
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:26,780
由于预算削减 我的初中音乐教师岗位
Due to budget cuts, my position as middle-school music teacher

46
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:27,680
被撤销了
has been eliminated,

47
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:30,613
所以我一直在当高中替补教师
So I've been working as a high-school sub.

48
00:01:30,613 --> 00:01:31,580
好耶
Ka-ching!

49
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:34,160
我从没想到还会收到"使命召唤"呢
I never know when I'll be summoned to swoop into action.

50
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:35,640
我有点像蝙蝠侠
I'm kind of like batman.

51
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:38,280
但我接到的不是蝙蝠求救图案 而是一通电话
But except for a bat-signal, I get a phone call.

52
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:39,900
是啊 你还是发现了点差异
Yeah, you found the one difference.

53
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,120
我也不想错过她的开学日
I hate to miss her first day,

54
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:43,760
但你能送莉莉去学校吗
but do you mind taking Lily to school?

55
00:01:43,771 --> 00:01:44,669
小卡 今天吗
Oh, Cam, today?

56
00:01:44,669 --> 00:01:46,400
我得准备跟查理的会面
I got to prep for my meeting with Charlie.

57
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,300
我跟他只有一小时会谈时间
I only get him for an hour

58
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:49,400
那还是趁着他在阿斯彭和卡波间的度假间隙
between his vacations in Aspen and Cabo.

59
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:50,860
你得去当面跟他对质
Okay, you need to confront him

60
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,800
告诉他 他那点无聊的中年危机
and tell him his pathetic little midlife crisis

61
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,460
会让你无法完成你的工作
is making it impossible for you to do your job.

62
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:57,620
因为他是个谦逊接受批评的人吗
Because he responds so well to criticism.

63
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,560
不 他会炒了我 然后我们就不得不在
No, he'll fire me, and then we'll end up

64
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:01,300
你家的谷仓里举行婚礼
having to get married in your family's barn.

65
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:02,700
我们得抓紧时间预定了
Oh, well, we need to book that soon

66
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:03,900
因为春天是方形舞季
because spring is hoedown season,

67
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:05,200
接着又是夏季的剧团下乡演出 所以...
And then you get right into summer stock, so...

68
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,040
我才不相信你说的
I don't believe any of that.

69
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,700
好了 如果要由我送莉莉 我得快点
All right, if I'm gonna take Lily, I need to hurry.

70
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,760
莉莉 甜心 快穿上衣服
Lily, sweetheart, let's get you dressed.

71
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,820
我衣服都穿好一小时了
Hey, I've been dressed for an hour.

72
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:14,160
快点 我可不能迟到 我会掉队的
Come on, I can't be late. I'll fall behind.

73
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:16,340
我有时总会忘记考虑她的亚洲人特性
Sometimes I forget to factor in the Asian.

74
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:32,800
伙计 我知道新学校会有点令人恐惧
Buddy, I know a new school can be scary,

75
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:33,780
所以给你点小建议
so a little advice --

76
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,900
你每碰到一个新朋友 就赞美对方几句
Every time you meet someone new, pay them a compliment.

77
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:40,760
比如 我喜欢你的头发
Like, um, "I love your hair."

78
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,800
腿法不错啊 你笑起来真美
"Awesome kicks." "You have a beautiful smile."

79
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:46,180
好了 老爸 我去跟那边那个大块头说
Okay, dad, I'll tell that big guy over there

80
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:47,440
他笑起来很美
that he's got a beautiful smile.

81
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:50,060
很好 皮肤啊 颧骨啊 随你怎么编
Fine. Skin, cheekbones, make it your own.

82
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:52,540
你能不能别一路跟着我进去
Um, could you maybe not walk me all the way in?

83
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:52,940
什么
What?

84
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:54,340
从这里开始我自己走就行
I've got it from here.

85
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:58,980
当然 好吧 跟你老爸抱
Sure. Yeah. Okay. Give your dad a --

86
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:00,380
去吧 艾丽克斯
Off you go. Alex!

87
00:03:04,036 --> 00:03:05,880
曼尼 你为什么这么安静
Ay, Manny, why are you so quiet?

88
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,160
因为高中开学第一天而紧张吗
Are you nervous because of your first day in high school?

89
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:10,400
老妈 在哥伦比亚待了一个夏天
Mom, after spending a summer in Colombia,

90
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,180
我已经脱胎换骨了
I'm a changed man.

91
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,580
天呐 你看到了什么
Oh, my God, what did you see?!

92
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:13,140
没什么
Nothing,

93
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:15,320
但我现在是个乘过喷气飞机跨国旅行的阔少了
but I am an international jet-setter now.

94
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,120
我很高端大气上档次
I'm sophisticated.

95
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:18,672
你觉得姑娘们会因为这个而注意你吗
And you think that the girls are gonna pick up on this?

96
00:03:18,672 --> 00:03:20,906
如果不行 我还有个"无人照顾的儿童"的标志
If not, I still have my "Unaccompanied minor" Sign.

97
00:03:20,906 --> 00:03:22,332
我真不敢相信
Ay, I cannot believe

98
00:03:22,332 --> 00:03:24,954
我的小宝贝都要上高中了
that my little baby's going to the high school.

99
00:03:24,954 --> 00:03:27,925
老妈 快住手 你这是让我出丑呢
Mom, stop. You're embarrassing me.

100
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:32,240
今天也是我开学第一天 我可以跟你抱抱
It's my first day, too. I could use a hug.

101
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,707
滚出
Go!

102
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,680
-你好啊 歌洛莉亚 -好啊 菲尔
- Hey, Gloria. - Hi, Phil.

103
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,380
高中开学第一天啊
First day of high school, huh?

104
00:03:37,562 --> 00:03:38,591
曼尼兴奋吗
Is Manny excited?

105
00:03:38,591 --> 00:03:41,537
他今天早上5点就起床熨衣服了
Ay, he was up at 5:00 in the morning, ironing.

106
00:03:42,011 --> 00:03:44,080
不过他郁闷的时候也这么做
Ay, but he does that, too, when he's depressed,

107
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,120
我也不知道是什么情况
so now I don't know.

108
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,700
卢克怎么样
How was Luke?

109
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:49,120
很好啊 他挺舍不得跟我告别的
Great. Yeah, he had a hard time saying goodbye.

110
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:52,880
但是不管怎样 我要买杯咖啡去
But, um, anyway, I think I'm gonna go get a cup of coffee.

111
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:55,040
-我能跟你一起去吗 -行啊
- Can I go with you? - Yeah.

112
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:58,120
老兄 我正在对美女发动攻势呢
Dude, I'm kind of working something here.

113
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,380
要几辆卡车
How many trucks would that take?

114
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,220
等我一会儿 弗雷德
Give me a minute, Fred.

115
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:06,640
新来的姑娘来了
New girl just walked in.

116
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,840
你这话真恶心 那是我女儿
That's disgusting. She's my daughter.

117
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:11,060
亲爱的 你看起来美极了
Sweetheart, you look terrific.

118
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:11,960
真的吗
Are you sure?

119
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:14,160
因为我还带了领一件衬衫在...在这里
'cause I have another blouse in -- in here.

120
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:16,260
里面只有这一样东西 衬衫和一副眼镜
It's the only thing in here, that and a pair of glasses

121
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:18,300
以防我需要读点什么 看起来聪明一点
In case I need to read something or look smarter.

122
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:18,960
放松
Relax.

123
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,620
今天是你第一天工作
It's your first day.

124
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,100
不会搞砸的 那是什么
Impossible to blow it. What are those?

125
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:24,760
饼干 我给工作人员做的
Oh, cookies -- I made them for the office.

126
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,860
大错误 弗雷德 再给我点时间
Huge mistake. Fred, two more seconds.

127
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:29,492
我这里出了点状况 把饼干放下
I got a situation here. Put the cookies down.

128
00:04:29,492 --> 00:04:31,120
-为什么 -你是管理层
- Why? - You're management.

129
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,360
那让你显得费尽心机
Makes you look desperate.

130
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:34,320
显得你很渴望让大家都喜欢你
Makes you look like you want everyone to like you.

131
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,440
我确实很想让大家都喜欢我
I do want everyone to like me.

132
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:36,940
你想让大家都尊重你
You want everyone to respect you.

133
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,589
你就得冷酷 树立距离感
You got to be tough. Keep your distance.

134
00:04:38,599 --> 00:04:41,000
也许我们是不同类型的管理人
Well, maybe we are different kinds of managers.

135
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,100
是啊 但你归我管 把饼干留下吧
Yeah, I'm yours. Just leave the cookies.

136
00:04:45,586 --> 00:04:48,140
瞧瞧你 我的一年级宝贝
Look at you, my big first-grader.

137
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:49,700
好了 我希望你交到很多朋友
All right, I want you to make so many friends

138
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,800
享受欢乐时光
and have so much fun.

139
00:04:50,810 --> 00:04:53,600
我得走了 迫不及待要去学习了
Got to go! I can't wait to learn!

140
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,020
-小心点 -什么
- Be careful! - What?

141
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:57,500
没什么
Nothing.

142
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:04,940
请不要迟到 快点 情况不错
Please do not be late. Let's go. Looking good.

143
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:06,040
布朗校长
Uh, uh, Principal Brown?

144
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,160
-什么事 -你好 我是卡梅隆·塔克
- Yes. - Hi. I'm Cameron Tucker.

145
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:08,340
我接到了电话 要我今天代课
I was called in to sub today.

146
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:10,460
对哦 你是来代替哈利老师的 你好
Oh, yeah, you're in for Mrs. Hurley. Hello.

147
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,240
-你好 -她得去康复中心戒瘾
- Hello. - She has come down with a sudden case of rehab.

148
00:05:13,586 --> 00:05:14,503
好好干吧
So do a good job

149
00:05:14,503 --> 00:05:15,989
这可能是个长期职位
'cause this could be a permanent position.

150
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,620
你就当自己是件结实的老牛仔背心吧
Well, prepare to feel like an old denim vest

151
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:19,631
因为我会亮瞎你的眼
because I'm about to "Be-dazzling" You.

152
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:22,100
我不知道那是什么意思 但好吧
I don't know what that means, but okay.

153
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:24,620
我教哪门课
So, what am I teaching?

154
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:26,082
高阶历史
A.P. History.

155
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:29,760
我十分想要那份工作
I desperately wanted that job.

156
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:30,780
但只有一个问题
There was just one problem --

157
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:32,080
我对历史知之甚少
I don't know much about history.

158
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,340
那你很了解生物吗
Do you know much biology?

159
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:34,040
别犯贱 米奇尔
Not now, Mitchell.

160
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,240
你的科学或者法语怎么样
What about your science book or the French you took?

161
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,100
你真走运我很爱你
You're lucky I love you.

162
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:38,860
我知道如果你也爱我
And I know that if you love me, too...

163
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:41,600
*世界将会多么美好*
*What a wonderful world this would be*

164
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,179
我真的摊上麻烦了
I really was in a jam, though.

165
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,980
我爸觉得树立冷酷疏远的权威形象
My dad thinks that he can motivate his workers

166
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:51,720
能激发员工的积极性
by being a cold, distant authority figure.

167
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:55,460
如果他的方法那么有效 回答我这个问题
Well, if his style is so effective, riddle me this --

168
00:05:55,834 --> 00:05:57,578
为什么我从来不听他的
why didn't I listen to him?

169
00:05:59,386 --> 00:06:00,327
大家好
Hey.

170
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,380
抱歉打扰了 我叫克莱尔
Hi. Sorry. I'm Claire.

171
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,780
今天是我第一天来上班 所以我来打个招呼
It's my first day, so I thought I'd say hi.

172
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:07,280
-你好 -太神奇了
- Oh. Hey. - Amazing.

173
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:10,660
你们居然真在冷水器旁边谈天说地
You guys are actually hanging out by the water cooler.

174
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:13,380
我得了口干症 长期口腔干燥
I have xerostomia. It's chronic dry mouth.

175
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,613
我 很抱歉
I'm -- I'm so sorry.

176
00:06:14,613 --> 00:06:18,610
我只是随口说说 你知道的 就像...
I-I-I-I was just doin' a thang, you know, like...

177
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:20,320
话说回来
Anyway,

178
00:06:21,753 --> 00:06:25,200
我办公室的大门一直为各位敞开
My door's always open... to everyone.

179
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,240
她是普里契特的女儿
That's Pritchett's daughter.

180
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,560
是的 但我不希望你们拘泥于我这个身份
Um, yeah, but I don't want you to think of me like that.

181
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:33,020
我是你们的朋友 是同事
I'm -- I'm a friend. I'm a colleague.

182
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:33,920
我就和你们一样
I'm just like you.

183
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:40,980
我是克莱尔 勤劳的工蜂
I'm Claire, you know -- worker bee, just...

184
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:42,700
见到你们真好
Great to meet you.

185
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,520
抱歉打扰了 回头见
Sorry to interrupt, and see you around.

186
00:06:45,327 --> 00:06:48,485
我必须得表演一下
I do -- I got to do this one.

187
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,160
我是谁
Who am I?

188
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,580
你们可以在我身体里挂衣服
You can hang your clothes in me.

189
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,574
克里斯托弗-步入式衣柜
Christopher walk-in closet.

190
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:04,560
什么情况
What is this?

191
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:07,300
二位 对不起 这里停业了 我们在拍广告
Oh, sorry, folks. It's closed. We're shooting a commercial.

192
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:08,620
真烦人
So annoying.

193
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,480
我们只想喝杯咖啡
Listen, we just want to get a cup of coffee.

194
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,300
其实我们还缺少两位群众演员
Actually, we're short a couple of extras.

195
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,580
你们愿意帮忙吗
How would you two like to be in it?

196
00:07:14,622 --> 00:07:16,729
-愿意 -听起来棒极了
- Yes! - That sounds amazing.

197
00:07:16,782 --> 00:07:19,132
我看见了两位老人
Hey, um, I see a couple of old people.

198
00:07:19,132 --> 00:07:21,281
这不是导尿管的广告吧
This isn't one of those catheter commercials, is it?

199
00:07:21,281 --> 00:07:22,520
如果广告描述的太详细
'Cause if it gets too descriptive,

200
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,220
我会浑身难受的
I'm gonna squirm.

201
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:24,880
我刚刚就抖了一下
I just did it to myself.

202
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:28,280
我尽全力备好了
I did my best to cram for my lecture

203
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,020
美国独立战争这堂课 但是
on the revolutionary war, but, ugh.

204
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:33,260
所有的名字和日期都十分枯燥
All those names and dates -- it's all so dry.

205
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:35,740
怎样才能制造戏剧效果呢
Where's the drama?

206
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:41,920
早安
Good morrow!

207
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:42,860
天啊
Oh, boy.

208
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:46,560
你们穿的是什么奇怪的服饰
Oh, what is all this strange garb you adorn?

209
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:49,240
你们是从加拿大省来的捕兽者吗
Are you trappers from the Canadian provinces?

210
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:51,340
你们是来卖海狸的吗
Are you here to sell your beavers?

211
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:53,260
你是谁啊
Who are you?

212
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:55,821
价值64便士的问题
The 64-pence question.

213
00:07:56,660 --> 00:08:00,120
我在独立战争期间 曾穿过特拉华州
I crossed the Delaware during the Revolutionary War.

214
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:04,780
我在福治河谷度过了寒冬
I spent a brutal winter in Valley Forge.

215
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:05,980
我是谁
Who am I?

216
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:07,922
我完全不知道
I-I have no idea.

217
00:08:07,922 --> 00:08:09,929
我发誓我不认识这人
I-I swear I don't know who this man is.

218
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:13,120
我当然是乔治·华盛顿啦
I'm George Washington, of course.

219
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,900
教学大纲上写着 我们应该学习
Our syllabus says we're supposed to cover

220
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:16,620
美国原著民在殖民主义开始前的状况
Native Americans on the eve of colonization.

221
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:19,760
是啊 美国原住民 印第安人
Yes. Native Americans. Indians!

222
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:22,240
威严和平的民族
A majestic, peaceful people,

223
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:25,220
他们依靠土地生存 看见垃圾时会哭泣
who lived off the land and cried when they saw litter.

224
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,900
课本上写的是部落之间常常发生战争
The textbook says many tribes were often at war,

225
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:29,323
朝秦暮楚 朝三...
with allegiances shifting all of the ti--

226
00:08:29,334 --> 00:08:30,746
朝三暮四
Shifting all the time!

227
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:34,960
那印第安人和殖民者到底是不是朋友
So, were the Indians friends with the Colonists or not?

228
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:35,940
问得好 是的
Ah! Yes.

229
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:37,080
我认识一个印第安人
I know one Indian

230
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:39,540
他和建筑工人 骑车人
who was friends with a construction worker, biker,

231
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:40,700
以及交警都是好朋友
and traffic cop.

232
00:08:41,798 --> 00:08:43,028
你们 没反应吗
Uh, do y-- nothing?

233
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:43,820
没搞错吧 居然没反应
Seriously, nothing?

234
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:46,160
你们的爹妈会喜欢刚刚那笑话的
Okay, your parents are gonna love that joke.

235
00:08:48,316 --> 00:08:51,360
好了 普里契特 我来了 你有半小时时间
Okay, Pritchett, I'm here. You got a half-hour.

236
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:53,180
我的直升飞机在楼顶上等着
I have my helicopter standing by on the roof.

237
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:54,466
楼顶上能停直升飞机吗
Is it even built for that?

238
00:08:54,466 --> 00:08:56,569
不能 所以你只有半小时
No. That's why you only have a half-hour.

239
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:57,780
我不确定时间够不够
Well, I'm not sure that's gonna be enough time.

240
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:58,700
我们要说好多事呢
We have a ton to cover.

241
00:08:58,700 --> 00:09:00,720
我们得谈谈新的租赁合同
We need to talk about new lease agreements

242
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,427
以及工人的薪资福利问题
and the workers' comp package.

243
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,260
只剩29分钟了 我好像听到了嘎吱声
29 minutes. I think I hear creaking.

244
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:06,980
爹地 我好无聊
Daddy, I'm bored.

245
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:08,720
我也是
Me, too.

246
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:10,740
所以我不该在假期之间来工作
This is why I shouldn't come into work between vacations.

247
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:12,240
你去坐在娜塔莉的桌子旁
Why don't you sit at Natalie's desk

248
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,680
假装是我的助理好吗 亲爱的
and pretend to be my assistant, sweetie?

249
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:17,120
抱歉 我侄女马上就来接走她
Sorry about that. My niece is coming to pick her up.

250
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:19,360
莉莉今天在学校出了场事故 她...
Lily had an incident at school today where she --

251
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:19,860
普里契特
Hey, Pritchett,

252
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:22,340
你又不是我想勾引的单身辣妈
you're not some hot single mom i'm trying to seduce,

253
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:23,900
我没必要听你唠叨你家小孩
so I don't need to hear about your kid.

254
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,740
有道理 好吧 租赁合同
Fair enough. So, lease agreements.

255
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:29,200
迈阿密那处房产有些推迟
Okay, I'm getting some push-back on the Miami location.

256
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:32,180
普里契特先生 有位海莉小姐找你
Mr. Pritchett, I have a Haley here to see you.

257
00:09:32,265 --> 00:09:33,028
好吧
Oh. Okay.

258
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:34,620
你好 亲爱的
Hi, sweetheart.

259
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:36,740
我在和我老板开会呢
I'm in the middle of a meeting with my boss,

260
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:38,500
万分感谢你来帮我
but thank you so much for helping me out.

261
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:39,200
没关系
No problem.

262
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,664
我上节课只给及格或不及格
My last class is a pass/fail.

263
00:09:40,664 --> 00:09:43,160
那是社区大学 所以肯定会及格
And it's community college, so it's pass.

264
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:45,240
你好 我是查理·宾汉姆
Hi. Charlie Bingham.

265
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:46,660
瞧瞧你美丽的双眸
Look at your eyes.

266
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:48,178
我看不到
Oh. I-I can't.

267
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:50,900
我喜欢你
I like you.

268
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:52,420
你觉得我的裤子怎么样
What do you think of these pants?

269
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:53,960
是我们的新款之一
It's part of our new collection.

270
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:56,420
有好多拉链啊
It's, uh, a lot of zippers.

271
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:57,000
太多了 是吧
It's too many, right?

272
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
当我坐直升机时 拉链都戳进了我的大腿
And they poke into my thigh when I'm in my helicopter.

273
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,140
因为我有直升飞机 没什么大不了的
'Cause I have a helicopter. It's not a big deal.

274
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:02,380
总之 谢谢你
Okay, so, anyway, thank you.

275
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:04,000
你好像很了解时尚
You seem to know a lot about fashion.

276
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:05,900
关于几件衣服的款式 我想问问你的意见
I'd like to get your opinion on a few things.

277
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:06,720
-当然啦 -可以吗
- Sure. - Yeah?

278
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,640
-可以 -其实不行 她得留下来照看莉莉
- Yeah. - Actually, no, she -- she needs to stay and watch Lily.

279
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:10,580
你去照看吧
Yeah, you can do that.

280
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:13,020
你好啊 小公主
Hey, princess. Hey.

281
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:14,320
我超爱小孩子
I love kids.

282
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:18,140
爹地的办公室
Daddy's office.

283
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:21,900
你讲话才像小女孩呢
You sound like a little girl.

284
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:26,500
你想见我吗
Hey, you wanted to see me?

285
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,120
谢谢你"凑空"过来
Thanks for "Bzzzing" By.

286
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,740
我希望你"木有"在忙呢
I hope you weren't in the middle of a "Thang."

287
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,220
好吧 刚刚我确实有点失控
Okay, that did get a little away from me.

288
00:10:32,220 --> 00:10:34,340
但说实话 我打破了坚冰
But to be fair, I broke the ice.

289
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,880
每个人都觉得你是个傻瓜
Everybody thinks you're a dummy.

290
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,740
不是每个人 不是的 实际上
Not everybody. No, as a matter of fact,

291
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:39,660
休息室有个人约我共进午餐呢
One of the guys in the break room asked me to lunch.

292
00:10:39,660 --> 00:10:40,830
-他名叫陶德 -别说是陶德啊
- His name is Todd. - Don't say Todd.

293
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:41,400
不是吧
Oh, no.

294
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:43,240
你不能和陶德一起共进午餐
You cannot go to lunch with Todd.

295
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:43,860
为什么不行
Why not?

296
00:10:43,980 --> 00:10:46,020
你不能和他有什么往来
You can't be associated with him.

297
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:47,160
直到一小时前
Up until an hour ago,

298
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,320
他的"办公室怪胎"身份都无人动摇
he was the office weirdo.

299
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:49,600
但他对我很好啊
But he was nice to me,

300
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,720
他还帮我装电脑呢
And he helped me set up my computer.

301
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,780
是啊 那就是他的工作 暂时是的
Yeah, that's his job. For now.

302
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:53,840
那是什么意思
What does that mean?

303
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:56,140
我一找到新的IT人才就会炒了他
I'm firing him as soon as I can find an I.T. Guy

304
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:57,180
只要那个人能准时上班
who shows up on time

305
00:10:57,180 --> 00:10:58,620
而且不会让办公室其他人觉得讨厌
and doesn't creep out the office.

306
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:01,420
我不能取消跟他的约定 他是唯一对我好的人
I can't cancel on the one person who was nice to me.

307
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:02,300
你可以取消 但你不会取消的
You can, but you won't,

308
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:04,540
因为你是那种会带饼干到办公室来的人
'cause you're the type of person who brings cookies to the office.

309
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:05,720
饼干哪儿去了
Where are they?

310
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:06,880
好了 没什么好说的了
Okay, we're done here.

311
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:10,200
好了 大伙儿 你们就装作随意交谈
Okay, folks, you're just having a normal conversation,

312
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:12,680
就像平常在咖啡店里那样 明白吗
a typical day in a coffee shop, all right?

313
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:13,360
明白
Roger that.

314
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:15,840
开始了哦 大家
Here we go, guys.

315
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:19,781
准备 开拍
And...action!

316
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:20,900
你最近怎么样 罗伊
How have you been, Roy?

317
00:11:20,912 --> 00:11:23,244
心情有点低落
Ah, a little down.

318
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:25,120
海伦和我真的很想念孩子们
Helen and I really miss the kids,

319
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:27,340
但我们现在没钱去探望他们
But we just can't afford to visit them right now.

320
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:30,420
-你们考虑过反向抵押贷款吗 -那是什么
- Have you considered a reverse mortgage? - What's that?

321
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:32,600
-你的房子是有产权的对吧 -咖啡真好喝啊
- You have equity in your home, right? - This coffee is delicious!

322
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,320
后面的二位 我们听到你们的声音了
All right, you two in the back, we can hear you,

323
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:36,700
你们能像演哑剧一样用手势对话吗
So just mime your conversation.

324
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:37,900
哑剧 哑剧 我懂的
Mime -- mime -- I knew that.

325
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:39,460
我刚刚就是那样做的 跟着我做就行了
I was already doing that, so just follow my lead.

326
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:40,980
好的 抱歉 我们再来一次
Okay, sorry, sorry. We'll do it again.

327
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:42,740
但我们的其他表现都可以吗
But everything else is okay?

328
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:45,120
你们还没做其他什么事
You haven't done anything else.

329
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:47,300
-所以是说可以吗 -重新开始
- So, yeah? - Back to one, guys.

330
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:49,180
开拍
Action.

331
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:51,000
你最近怎么样 罗伊
How have you been, Roy?

332
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,120
心情有点低落
Ah, a little down.

333
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,660
海伦和我真的很想念孩子们
Helen and I really miss the kids,

334
00:11:54,740 --> 00:11:56,820
但我们现在没钱去探望他们
But we just can't afford to visit them right now.

335
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:59,600
-你们考虑过反向抵押贷款吗 -那是什么
- Have you considered a reverse mortgage? - What's that?

336
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,600
你的房子是有产权的对吧
You have equity in your home, right?

337
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:02,680
-当然了 -他们在搞什么呢
- Sure, we do. - What are they doing?

338
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:04,560
她是在假装接电话吗
Is she answering an imaginary phone?

339
00:12:05,460 --> 00:12:06,980
那简直好得令人难以置信啊
Oh, that sounds too good to be true.

340
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,160
你可以不用听我的
Don't take my word for it.

341
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:10,300
接下来亨利·维克纳会给你做更详细的介绍
Here's Henry Winkler to tell you more.

342
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,040
好了 停
Okay, cut.

343
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,760
后面的那一对
Couple in the back.

344
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,800
在 不 我懂了 再大点声吗
Yep. No, I know. I know. Bigger?

345
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:18,940
美国原著民和殖民者
The native Americans and the settlers

346
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:22,200
对土地所有权的观念完全不同
had two completely different ideas of land ownership.

347
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,640
最终 这些不同将引发战争
Eventually, these differences would lead to war.

348
00:12:26,425 --> 00:12:29,065
快看 我都起鸡皮疙瘩了
Oh. Look, goose bumps.

349
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:33,620
好了 就到这儿吧 下课
Okay, yes. Uh, class dismissed.

350
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:36,540
我们做到了
We did it!

351
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:39,580
谢谢你半路拔刀相助 我保证
Thank you so much for stepping in. Oh, and I promise,

352
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:41,460
明天我一定课前做好充分准备
Tomorrow, I will do my best to be more prepared.

353
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:43,480
明天吗 哈利老师不是回来了吗
Tomorrow? Why won't Mrs. Hurley be back?

354
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,160
我也不想说出这么无礼的话
Well, I don't want to be indelicate,

355
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:47,700
但好消息是 我可能会成为你的专职老师
But the good news is, is I might be your permanent teacher.

356
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:50,580
-我不希望你成为我的专职老师 -怎么
- I don't want you to be my permanent teacher. - Oh, what?

357
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:51,820
你更希望一个大酒鬼来当你的老师吗
You'd rather have a raging alcoholic?

358
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:52,660
听好了
Listen to me.

359
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:55,300
我孜孜不倦地学习 才取得这么好的成绩
I've worked nonstop to build the perfect academic record,

360
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:56,920
我可不会让你给毁了
And I'm not going to let you screw it up now.

361
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:59,180
我160天后就要进行高阶考试了
I have an A.P. Test in 160 days,

362
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:00,720
我必须名列前茅
and I need to ace it.

363
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,660
你能助我登上顶峰吗
Can you get me there or not?

364
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:06,200
我可以像阿拉摩的勇士一般重振旗鼓
I can rally like the brave men of the Alamo.

365
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:08,820
你知道阿拉摩的勇士全死光了吧
You do realize that all the men of the alamo died?

366
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,200
他们全死了
They all died!

367
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:16,160
露希年长一些 所以她觉得自己就是老大
Ruthie's older, so she thinks she's the boss.

368
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:18,760
但对于一个小家伙来说 斯顿自有一套
But for a little guy, Stu holds his own.

369
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:20,420
他们有时候挺难伺候的
They can be a handful.

370
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:23,580
但是 他们总让我笑得肚子疼
But, god, they make me laugh so hard, you know?

371
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:26,760
我不知道你连乌龟的性别都可以区分开呢
I did not know you could even tell the gender of a turtle.

372
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,360
那当然了
Oh, yeah.

373
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:30,720
那叫"乌龟辨雌雄"大法 总共有8步
It's called "Sexing the turtle," And it's an eight-step process.

374
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,780
现在我们假装你的手就是一只乌龟
Now, let's pretend your hand is a turtle.

375
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,035
-好的 -你要把它翻过身来
- Okay. - What you do is you flip it over.

376
00:13:34,211 --> 00:13:35,828
然后你要仔细瞧瞧它的...
And then you have to look right into --

377
00:13:35,828 --> 00:13:38,044
好吧 我懂了 我懂了 我想明白了
Oh, okay. I get it. I get it. I think I get it.

378
00:13:38,044 --> 00:13:39,926
我懂的 我的说教太无聊了 对吧
Oh. I know. I'm droning on, aren't I?

379
00:13:42,308 --> 00:13:44,180
停下 求你快停下
Please, stop. Please stop!

380
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:45,200
你没有啦 你没有啦
You're not. You're not.

381
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:47,540
我就是的 不过我的家庭情况介绍得够多了
I am. But enough about my family.

382
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,360
跟我说说你的家庭吧
Tell me about yours.

383
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:50,480
好啊 我丈夫菲尔是个房地产中介
All right, well, my husband Phil's a realtor.

384
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:52,200
真巧啊 我刚好想买房呢
That's funny. I'm buying a house.

385
00:13:52,380 --> 00:13:53,600
为什么 什么时候
Why? When?

386
00:13:53,612 --> 00:13:55,940
实际上 我们今天就要进行最后的看房
Actually, we have the final walk-through today,

387
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:56,800
明天就签合同了
Sign the papers tomorrow.

388
00:13:57,660 --> 00:13:59,800
那 那可是件大事 陶德
Th-that's a really big deal, Todd.

389
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,880
是啊 而且对我们也挺艰难的
Yeah, and it's a bit of a stretch for us, too,

390
00:14:01,890 --> 00:14:04,260
但是 不行 现在时机正好
But, uh, no, the time is right.

391
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,180
我们 我们一定要买
We're just -- we're gonna do it.

392
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:07,360
"我们"指的是你和乌龟们吗
"We" is you and the turtles?

393
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:09,560
不 是我和我妻子
No, me and my wife.

394
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:11,140
妻...我很抱歉
A w-- I'm sorry.

395
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:12,360
你没说你有妻子啊 那太棒了
You didn't mention your wife. That's great.

396
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:15,420
我猜她的工作一定高端又高薪吧
I bet she's got a big, fancy, high-paying job, right?

397
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,340
她正在攻读硕士学位
Uh, she's getting her master's.

398
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:18,400
-哪方面的 -拉丁文
- In? - Latin.

399
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:20,720
陶德呀
Oh, Todd.

400
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:26,100
现在或许不是买房的最佳时机
This may not be the best time to buy a house.

401
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:28,420
我也不想做坏人 来跟你说这些
I hate to be the one to break this to you --

402
00:14:28,420 --> 00:14:29,707
不不不 我来买单
Oh. No, no, no, no, I got this.

403
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:31,100
不 不用了
No, you don't.

404
00:14:33,637 --> 00:14:35,026
大家预备
Stand by, everyone.

405
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,280
我真觉得我上一条拍得特别好
I really felt like I nailed that last one.

406
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:40,460
我还是觉得很不入戏
I still feel so stiff.

407
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,180
我都不知道该假装说什么才好
I don't know what to pretend saying.

408
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:45,180
你想得太多了 就从你的现实生活出发就好
You're thinking too much. Just draw from your own life.

409
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:46,480
比如 你今天过得怎么样
Like, how was your day today?

410
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:49,780
糟透了 我的亲儿子不想跟我拥抱
Lousy. My own son didn't want to hug me.

411
00:14:50,260 --> 00:14:51,520
好吧 就用上这种情绪
Okay, so use that.

412
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:53,640
我的角色 叫斯蒂芬·威尔逊医生
My character, Dr. Stephen Wilson,

413
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:56,440
也很伤心 因为他儿子不肯听他的建议
Is also sad because his son wouldn't take his advice

414
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:59,160
而且他想在距学校一个街区远的地方就下车
And he wanted to be dropped off a block away from school.

415
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:01,720
他能理解他的女儿们这么做
He expected that from his daughters

416
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,000
他以为他的儿子会不一样呢
But thought his son would be different.

417
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:04,960
那太可悲了
That's so sad.

418
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:07,160
但斯蒂芬医生是不会让这件事
But Dr. Stephen wilson is not going to let that

419
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:08,360
毁了他和情人的早餐时光
ruin breakfast with his mistress.

420
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:14,200
其实 或许我们现在是时候
You know, maybe it's just time for us to --

421
00:15:14,555 --> 00:15:17,016
放开他们的手了
to accept that we have to let them go.

422
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:19,740
或许是吧
Maybe it is.

423
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:23,940
好了 大家 开始了 摄像机要开拍了
Okay, everyone, here we go. We're rolling.

424
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:26,620
开始
And action!

425
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,140
你最近怎么样 罗伊
How have you been, Roy?

426
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:29,794
心情有点低落
Ah, a little down.

427
00:15:29,794 --> 00:15:31,680
海伦和我真的很想念孩子们
Helen and I really miss the kids,

428
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,880
但我们现在没钱去探望他们
But we just can't afford to visit them right now.

429
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:37,800
-你们考虑过反向抵押贷款吗 -那是什么
- Have you considered a reverse mortgage? - What's that?

430
00:15:38,335 --> 00:15:41,158
你的房子是有产权的对吧
Uh, you have equity in your home, right?

431
00:15:41,158 --> 00:15:42,240
-当然 -请你别哭
- Sure, we do. - Please, no crying.

432
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:43,860
你哭我也想哭了
You're gonna make me cry, too.

433
00:15:43,870 --> 00:15:46,400
本质上来说就是银行买下了你的房子
Well, essentially the bank buys your house.

434
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,840
但你依然可以住在里面
But you still get to live in it.

435
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,940
那简直好得令人难以置信啊
That sounds too good to be true.

436
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,480
你可以不用听我的
Don't take my word for it.

437
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:53,820
接下来亨利·维克纳会给你做更详细的介绍
Here's Henry Winkler to tell us more.

438
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:57,460
我可不想让方奇看到我这个样子
I don't want the Fonz to see me like this.

439
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:01,240
这件是样品 可以抵挡住
It's a prototype. It can withstand

440
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,160
地球上最极端的温度
the most extreme temperatures on the planet.

441
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:05,660
防水面料 可以去除汗水
It's waterproof, and it wicks sweat.

442
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,140
那也会令女人却步
It also repels women.

443
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:09,000
我知道 我讨厌这件 今晚我就烧掉
I know. I hate it. I'll burn it tonight!

444
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,040
事实上 这个烧不掉
Aah! Actually, it doesn't burn.

445
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:13,680
好啦 我们继续说租赁合同
Anyway, if we could get back to the lease agreements here.

446
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:15,900
你太厉害了 你觉得该怎么改
You're amazing. How would you fix it?

447
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:16,800
太宽松了
It's too boxy.

448
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:18,900
也许可以改成这样
Probably have to take it in here...

449
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:20,080
-没错 -还有这里
- Right. - ...and here.

450
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:22,032
我健身健得有些过了
Yeah, I probably overdo it in the gym.

451
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,280
该死的7%的身体脂肪
Stupid 7% body fat.

452
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,860
好吧 继续工作
Okay, so getting back to work.

453
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,620
我们在工作 为什么要工作
We are working. Why are we working?!

454
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:31,324
我得去卡波了 你想和我一起去吗
I got to go to Cabo. Hey, you want to come with me?

455
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:33,140
我从未去过卡波
Oh, I've, uh, never been to Cabo.

456
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:35,200
她不会去卡波 因为你老得能当她爹了
Yeah, she's not going to cabo 'cause she's half your age.

457
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:36,780
-你多大了 -谁在乎这个
- How old are you? - Who cares?

458
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:38,000
很快 我就会面如二十少年郎
Pretty soon, I'm gonna look 20.

459
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:40,520
我一直在密封蛋内冥想[类似太空舱]
I've been meditating in one of those pressurized eggs.

460
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:41,740
如果我去卡波
Well, if I went to cabo,

461
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:43,400
睡眠情况会是怎样的
what would the sleeping situation be?

462
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:44,520
没什么时间睡
Not much.

463
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:46,680
好了 够了 调戏到此为止
Okay, no, that is enough! No! No!

464
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:47,800
她是我的外甥女
She is my niece!

465
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:48,540
明白吗
Okay?

466
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:50,880
你这种可悲的中年危机
This pathetic midlife crisis of yours

467
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,120
危害到了公司
is -- is hurting the company,

468
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:54,780
我已经厌倦了给你擦屁股
and I'm getting so sick of cleaning up your messes.

469
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:57,660
你需要集中精神 你的行为要与年龄相符
Y-you need to focus and you need to start acting your age --

470
00:16:57,660 --> 00:17:01,190
你真正的年龄 而不是"蛋内"年龄
Your -- your real age, not your egg age.

471
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:06,700
通常来说 有人跟我这样说话 我会炒掉他
Normally, if someone talked to me that way, I'd fire him.

472
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:11,520
但我尊重你的诚实 尊重你的激情
But I respect your honesty. I respect your passion.

473
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:15,040
和我一样 我也是一个很有激情的男人
It's like me. I'm a very passionate man.

474
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:15,640
集中精神做正事
Just focus.

475
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:17,460
你说得对 你说得对
You're right. You're right. You're right. You're right.

476
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:19,200
那个嘎吱声是怎么回事
What's that creaking?

477
00:17:22,504 --> 00:17:24,369
预备 开球
Hut! Hike!

478
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:25,840
你跑错方向了
Oh, hey, you're going the wrong way!

479
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:27,500
方向错了 不是
That's the wrong way! No!

480
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,260
等等 对不起 你是对的
Wait. I'm sorry. You're right.

481
00:17:30,079 --> 00:17:32,263
打扰下 布朗校长
Uh, excuse me, principal Brown.

482
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:35,060
妈呀 大多数代课老师就在课上放部电影算了
Yikes. You know, most subs just play a movie.

483
00:17:35,420 --> 00:17:36,940
好啦 来点不同的 同学们
All right, do something different, guys.

484
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:39,820
听我说 我不能做历史老师
Uh, listen, I-I can't be your history teacher.

485
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:42,980
那些孩子学习非常努力 他们值得拥有
Those kids work so hard, and they deserve someone

486
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:47,240
真才实学 并且可以激励他们的老师 所以
who knows the material and can inspire them, so...

487
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:48,160
随你吧
If you say so.

488
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:49,540
我想问下
Hey, I was wondering,

489
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:50,700
你这是在训练什么战术
what kind of play was that you were running?

490
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:51,760
是侧攻吗
Was that supposed to be a slant?

491
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:53,360
高一的教练辞职了
Our freshman coach quit.

492
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,620
我这是变相在做保姆
I'm just a glorified babysitter.

493
00:17:55,340 --> 00:17:57,180
接球手需要学习跑位
Well, your receiver needs to learn to run his routes,

494
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:58,800
否则四分卫不可能把球传给他
or the quarterback's never gonna be able to hit him.

495
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,760
-我在大学时打过校队 -好的
- I-I played in college. - Oh. Okay.

496
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,560
泰勒 你需要学习跑位
Hey, Tyler, you need to learn to run your routes.

497
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:03,800
什么位
What routes?

498
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:05,940
对 什么位
Yeah, what routes?

499
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:08,880
在这里就位
Well, you're gonna line up here.

500
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:10,620
跑三步
Take three steps.

501
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:12,460
一二三 到这里
One, two, three -- plant right,

502
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,420
左45度跑向球场
Open left 45 degrees up the field.

503
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:15,900
不如再来一次
Okay, why don't we try it again?

504
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:17,360
再来一次
Try it again! Tip!

505
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:18,720
投球时要用力 18号
Put some zip on the ball, 18!

506
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,655
预备 开球
Hut, hut, hike!

507
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:22,360
扔给他
Hit him!

508
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:26,440
有进步 做得好 再来一次
Better. Better. Good job. Circle back up.

509
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:28,720
总之 感谢你给我这个机会
All right, anyway, thank you for the opportunity.

510
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:30,440
你想接管这支球队吗
Hey, hey, how would you like to take over this team?

511
00:18:30,833 --> 00:18:33,320
这个提议真有趣
Well, well, that's an interesting offer.

512
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,500
-工资多少 -没有
- How much does it pay? - Nothing.

513
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:35,400
你确定吗
Are you firm on that?

514
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:37,640
确定 但现在有体育老师的空缺
Yeah, but there's a gym-teacher position available.

515
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,360
-你做教练这活儿就归你了 -我可以穿短裤吗
- It's all yours if you coach. - Can I wear shorts?

516
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:40,720
可以 还有口哨给你
Yeah, and you get a whistle, too.

517
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,340
我穿短裤时总是有人对我吹口哨
Oh, I always get a whistle when I wear shorts.

518
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:44,340
我谦卑地接受您给的这份工作
I humbly accept your offer.

519
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:47,138
集合 同学们 来吧 快点
Huddle up, boys! Let's go! Hustle!

520
00:18:47,138 --> 00:18:49,497
你知道快点是什么意思吗 10号
Do you know what hustle means, 10?!

521
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:50,960
没那么糟糕
It really wasn't bad.

522
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:53,300
等你了解他 就会知道陶德是个非常有趣的人
Todd is a very interesting guy when you get to know him.

523
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,680
他给你讲了他的乌龟吗 小露露和斯坦
Did he tell you about his turtles, little Lulu and Stan?

524
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,980
是露希和斯顿
Ruthie and Stu.

525
00:18:56,980 --> 00:18:57,921
他取了这名字吗
That's the name he picks?

526
00:18:57,932 --> 00:19:00,518
乌龟斯"炖" 白痴
"Turtle stew"? Idiot!

527
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:02,880
出了点小状况
Well, there was one little situation that came up,

528
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:04,580
但我觉得我处理得很好
but I think I handled it pretty well.

529
00:19:04,740 --> 00:19:06,320
-他准备做一个大的... -等等
- He's about to make, um, kind of a big -- Hold on.

530
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:08,160
玛格丽特 我为什么不能登录
Margaret, why can't I log in here?

531
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:10,840
我的电脑出什么问题了
What's wrong with my computer?

532
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:12,440
整个系统都挂了
The whole system's down.

533
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:15,540
看不到文档 也上不了网
No one can access files. We can't get online.

534
00:19:15,620 --> 00:19:16,180
陶德在哪里
Where's Todd?

535
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:19,560
到处都找不到他 他的丰田车也没看到了
We can't find him anywhere, and his yaris is gone.

536
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:21,592
-我的文档呢 -搞什么鬼
- Where are my files?! - What the hell?

537
00:19:21,611 --> 00:19:24,605
这事我可能知道一点原因
I-I might know a little something about this.

538
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,360
你做了什么
What did you do?

539
00:19:27,581 --> 00:19:30,329
告诉陶德你打算炒掉他
Kind of told Todd that you were gonna fire him.

540
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:31,420
-什么 -我必须说
- What?! - I had to.

541
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:32,920
爸 他准备买房子
Dad, he's about to buy a house.

542
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,080
但他没什么意见
But he was fine with it.

543
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:35,460
他拥抱了我 谢了我
He hugged me and thanked me

544
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:37,943
告诉我这让他有时间早做安排
and told me that it gave him time to make a plan.

545
00:19:42,234 --> 00:19:45,246
先生们 今天是全新的开始
Gentlemen, today is a new beginning.

546
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,440
新的开始可能很可怕
And that can be scary.

547
00:19:49,168 --> 00:19:52,000
第一天还好吗 阔少
How did it go, Mr. Jet-setter?

548
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,340
很好 非常好
Good. Really good.

549
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:55,940
你想谈谈吗
Do you want to talk about it?

550
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:56,660
不想
No.

551
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:03,560
我对你们的要求 也许你们现在不太明白
I'm gonna ask things of you that may not make sense right now.

552
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:04,480
明天见 卢克
See you tomorrow, Luke.

553
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,700
除非我先见到你
Not if I see you first.

554
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:08,160
就是这样 笑容多灿烂
There it is! There's that smile.

555
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:11,020
但总有一天会懂的
But they will.

556
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:12,600
-老爸 -小家伙
- Hey, dad. - Hey, buddy.

557
00:20:16,696 --> 00:20:18,527
-校园里不要勾肩搭背 -好的
- We're at school. - Yep.

558
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,340
没人可以保证必然胜利
Success is not guaranteed.

559
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,800
胜利不是唾手可得的
It is not handed to you.

560
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:25,960
要争取才会有胜利
Success is earned.

561
00:20:28,942 --> 00:20:30,598
数据输入得怎么样
How's that data entry going?

562
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:32,320
很好 已经到1998年了
Good. I am up to 1998.

563
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:35,900
那时候我做这份工作差不多已经20年了
Ah, that's when I'd already been doing the job 20 years.

564
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,420
也许我应该听你的
So maybe I should listen to you?

565
00:20:38,532 --> 00:20:40,040
那样你就可以提早回家了
Get you home a lot earlier.

566
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:40,820
谢谢你 老板
Thanks, boss.

567
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:45,360
今天 我们在开拓一条新的道路 同学们
Today, we are forging a new path, people!

568
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:49,340
唯一能让我们恐惧的 就是恐惧本身
The only thing we have to fear is fear itself!

569
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:50,240
总统名言对应错位
Wrong president.

570
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:52,360
-给我推 -遵旨
- Just keep pushing! - Okay.
